Complex human-robot interaction environments often imply a varying number of sound sources.
Hence, at a given time, the room may be completely silent.
On the other hand, multiple concurrent sources of different kinds can be active simultaneously.
The current section presents our investigation of a multi-source localization framework that will give our acoustic agent additional flexibility.
We showcase a deep neural network implemented and trained on a challenging custom dataset, collected using our simulator.
This approach complements the initial investigation on single-source localization.
